{"id": "tea:ratnavali:1.26", "source": "src:ratnavali", "location": {"ref": "1.26", "chapter": "1", "verse": "26"}, "paraphrase": "'I am not, I will not be, I have nothing, I will have nothing' — this terrifies the childish and ends fear for the wise.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "powers-experiences"], "original": {"text": "nāsmyahaṃ na bhaviṣyāmi na me 'sti na bhaviṣyati / iti bālasya saṃtrāsaḥ paṇḍitasya bhayakṣayaḥ", "script": "IAST", "edition": "Ratnāvalī, GRETIL e-text after Vaidya (sources_raw/dcs/corpus/GRETIL/sa_nAgArjuna-ratnAvalI.txt)", "licence": "e-text: Digital Sanskrit Buddhist Canon / DCS / GRETIL; root text public domain"}, "concepts": ["cpt:fear-of-emptiness"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:ratnavali:1.28", "source": "src:ratnavali", "location": {"ref": "1.28", "chapter": "1", "verse": "28"}, "paraphrase": "'I exist' and 'mine exists' are false in the ultimate sense, for neither is found through knowing things as they really are.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "consciousness-mind"], "original": {"text": "astyahaṃ mama cāstīti mithyaitatparamārthibhiḥ / yathābhūtaparijñānānna bhavatyubhayaṃ yataḥ", "script": "IAST", "edition": "Ratnāvalī, GRETIL e-text after Vaidya (sources_raw/dcs/corpus/GRETIL/sa_nAgArjuna-ratnAvalI.txt)", "licence": "e-text: Digital Sanskrit Buddhist Canon / DCS / GRETIL; root text public domain"}, "terms": ["trm:ahamkara", "trm:mamakara"], "disputes": ["dsp:is-there-a-self"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:ratnavali:1.3-4", "source": "src:ratnavali", "location": {"ref": "1.3-4", "chapter": "1", "verse": "3-4"}, "paraphrase": "First comes the dharma of higher status, afterwards definite goodness arises, for having obtained higher status one comes gradually to definite goodness. Higher status is held to be happiness, definite goodness liberation; in brief their means are faith and wisdom.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["action", "knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:abhyudaya-naihsreyasa"], "paths": ["pth:ratnavali-two-goods"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:ratnavali:1.35", "source": "src:ratnavali", "location": {"ref": "1.35", "chapter": "1", "verse": "35"}, "paraphrase": "As long as there is grasping at the aggregates there is grasping at 'I'; where there is 'I'-making there is action, and from action again birth.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "causal", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "consciousness-mind"], "original": {"text": "skandhagrāho yāvadasti tāvadevāhamityapi / ahaṃkāre sati punaḥ karma janma tataḥ punaḥ", "script": "IAST", "edition": "Ratnāvalī, GRETIL e-text after Vaidya (sources_raw/dcs/corpus/GRETIL/sa_nAgArjuna-ratnAvalI.txt)", "licence": "e-text: Digital Sanskrit Buddhist Canon / DCS / GRETIL; root text public domain"}, "terms": ["trm:ahamkara", "trm:skandha"], "obstacles": ["obs:ahamkara-mamakara", "obs:satkayadrsti"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:ratnavali:1.36", "source": "src:ratnavali", "location": {"ref": "1.36", "chapter": "1", "verse": "36"}, "paraphrase": "This wheel of saṃsāra with its three paths, without beginning, middle or end, whirls like a firebrand's circle, each part the cause of the others.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "causal", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "world-fate"], "original": {"text": "trivartmaitadanādyantamadhyaṃ saṃsāramaṇḍalam / alātamaṇḍalaprakhyaṃ bhramatyanyonyahetukam", "script": "IAST", "edition": "Ratnāvalī, GRETIL e-text after Vaidya (sources_raw/dcs/corpus/GRETIL/sa_nAgArjuna-ratnAvalI.txt)", "licence": "e-text: Digital Sanskrit Buddhist Canon / DCS / GRETIL; root text public domain"}, "terms": ["trm:samsara", "trm:alatacakra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:ratnavali:1.42", "source": "src:ratnavali", "location": {"ref": "1.42", "chapter": "1", "verse": "42"}, "paraphrase": "Nirvāṇa is not even non-existence — how could it be existence? The ending of the conceptions of existence and non-existence is called nirvāṇa.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "apophatic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "original": {"text": "na cābhāvo 'pi nirvānaṃ kuta eva tasya bhāvatā / bhāvābhāvaparāmarśakṣayo nirvāṇamucyate", "script": "IAST", "edition": "Ratnāvalī, GRETIL e-text after Vaidya (sources_raw/dcs/corpus/GRETIL/sa_nAgArjuna-ratnAvalI.txt)", "licence": "e-text: Digital Sanskrit Buddhist Canon / DCS / GRETIL; root text public domain"}, "concepts": ["cpt:nirvana-in-madhyamaka"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:ratnavali:1.5", "source": "src:ratnavali", "location": {"ref": "1.5", "chapter": "1", "verse": "5"}, "paraphrase": "Through faith one relies on the Dharma, through wisdom one truly knows; of the two wisdom is chief, but faith goes first.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "devotion"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["practice"], "terms": ["trm:sraddha", "trm:prajna"], "paths": ["pth:ratnavali-two-goods"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:ratnavali:1.61-62", "source": "src:ratnavali", "location": {"ref": "1.61-62", "chapter": "1", "verse": "61-62"}, "paraphrase": "Ask the world, with its Sāṃkhyas, Vaiśeṣikas, Nirgranthas and proponents of the person and the aggregates, whether it teaches what passes beyond 'is' and 'is not'; therefore know that passing beyond existence and non-existence is the Dharma's special heritage, called profound, the nectar of the Buddhas' teaching.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["dispute", "ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:middle-way", "cpt:madhyamaka-critique-of-samkhya"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:ratnavali:1.8-10", "source": "src:ratnavali", "location": {"ref": "1.8-10", "chapter": "1", "verse": "8-10"}, "paraphrase": "Non-killing, not stealing, avoiding others' spouses, restraint from false, divisive, harsh and idle speech, and avoiding covetousness, malice and nihilistic views are the ten white paths of action, the black being their opposites; not drinking alcohol, right livelihood, non-harming, respectful giving, honouring the honourable and love — this in brief is the dharma.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics"], "concepts": ["cpt:ten-virtuous-paths"], "terms": ["trm:ahimsa", "trm:dana"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:ratnavali:2.1", "source": "src:ratnavali", "location": {"ref": "2.1", "chapter": "2", "verse": "1"}, "paraphrase": "Just as a plantain tree, when split apart with all its parts, is nothing at all, so a person, when split apart with the elements, is nothing at all.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "body-layers"], "original": {"text": "kadalī pāṭitā yadvanniḥśeṣāvayavaiḥ saha / na kiṃcitpuruṣastadvatpāṭitaḥ saha dhātubhiḥ", "script": "IAST", "edition": "Ratnāvalī, GRETIL e-text after Vaidya (sources_raw/dcs/corpus/GRETIL/sa_nAgArjuna-ratnAvalI.txt)", "licence": "e-text: Digital Sanskrit Buddhist Canon / DCS / GRETIL; root text public domain"}, "concepts": ["cpt:self-as-dependent-designation"], "disputes": ["dsp:is-there-a-self"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:ratnavali:3.12-13", "source": "src:ratnavali", "location": {"ref": "3.12-13", "chapter": "3", "verse": "12-13"}, "paraphrase": "The form bodies of the Buddhas arise from the collection of merit; the truth body, in brief, is born from the collection of wisdom.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "causal", "naya": null, "path": ["action", "knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:two-accumulations"], "terms": ["trm:dharmakaya"], "notes": "Verse numbers from memory; to be checked against the text.", "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:ratnavali:4.86", "source": "src:ratnavali", "location": {"ref": "4.86", "chapter": "4", "verse": "86"}, "paraphrase": "Non-arising is taught in the Mahāyāna, extinction for others — emptiness; since extinction and non-arising are one in meaning, (the Mahāyāna) should be accepted.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["dispute"], "disputes": ["dsp:mahayana-as-buddhavacana"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:ratnavali:4.94-96", "source": "src:ratnavali", "location": {"ref": "4.94-96", "chapter": "4", "verse": "94-96"}, "paraphrase": "As a grammarian may even teach the alphabet, so the Buddha taught the Dharma to his disciples according to what they could bear: to some a Dharma for turning away from evil, to some for achieving merit, to some one based on duality, to some one not based on duality — profound, frightening to the fearful, having emptiness and compassion as its essence, the means of achieving awakening.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:graded-teaching"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
